# Day 30

## Experiment Title

Creating a Node.js and MongoDB Application using Docker Compose


## Objective

To understand how Docker Compose can be used to deploy a Node.js application with a MongoDB database service.


## Theory

Modern applications often use multiple services working together. Docker Compose simplifies the deployment of such applications by allowing all services to be configured inside a single YAML file.

A Node.js application can communicate with a MongoDB database container through Docker networking. Docker Compose automatically manages service communication, container creation, and application execution.


## Requirements

Docker Desktop

Docker Compose

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open Docker Desktop and verify that Docker services are running properly.

Create a Docker Compose configuration file for Node.js and MongoDB services.

Configure the required application and database settings.

Start the Docker Compose application.

Verify that both containers are running successfully.

Check the communication between the Node.js application and MongoDB database.


## Output

Node.js and MongoDB containers were deployed successfully using Docker Compose.

The application connected successfully with the MongoDB database container.

Docker Compose managed container communication and execution properly.


## Result

Successfully created and deployed a Node.js and MongoDB application using Docker Compose.
